# Day in Review

Day in Review answers the question "what happened on this day?". It shows one
day in detail: glucose, insulin, carbs, and each decision of your automated
insulin delivery (AID) system, if you use one.

<Video id="day-in-review" />

## What it shows

### The day in numbers

- **The range bar** shows how the day's readings divide across five ranges:
  very low, low, in range, high and very high. Move the pointer over the bar to
  see each percentage.
- **The figures** under the bar give the **Mean**, **Median**, **Std Dev**,
  **CV**, **Range** (lowest to highest), **GMI** and the number of
  **Readings** for the day.
- **The insulin ring** shows the day's insulin, split into bolus and basal.
  Select a bolus in the ring to open it. Under the ring are the **Total Carbs**,
  the number of **Manual boluses** and the number of **Automatic boluses**.

### Blood Glucose

The chart shows the whole day, from midnight to midnight, with your treatments.
It is the same chart as in the [Readings](/docs/reports/readings) report.

### The time scrubber and the APS decision

If your AID system sends its decisions, a time scrubber shows under the chart.
The **APS Decision** card shows the decision at the time the scrubber points
to:

- **IOB** (insulin on board), split into basal and bolus, and **COB** (carbs
  on board).
- **Current BG**, **Eventual BG** (the glucose the system predicted) and
  **Target**.
- **Sensitivity**, as a percentage.
- A badge that says **Enacted** if the system acted, or **Suggested** if it did
  not. An enacted decision also shows the **Temp Basal** rate it set, and any
  **Auto-bolus**.

### Treatments Timeline

The table lists every treatment of the day, with its **Time**, **Type**,
**Carbs** and **Insulin**. Select a column name to sort by that column. Use
**All Types** to show one type of treatment only.

The app shows glucose values in mmol/L if you chose mmol/L.

## How to use it

The report opens on today. To open another day, you can also select a day in
the [Year Overview](/docs/reports/year-overview), or a time in the tooltip of a
glucose chart.

To step through the decisions of your AID system:

1. Under the chart, move the scrubber to a time. The **APS Decision** card
   shows the decision at that time.
2. To go to the start of the day, select **Go to start**. You can also press
   Home.
3. To move 5 minutes at a time, select the step buttons, or press the left and
   right arrow keys.
4. To play the day, select **Play**, or press Space.

To see another day:

1. Select the left arrow next to the date to go back one day.
2. Select the right arrow to go forward one day.

To correct a treatment, select its row in **Treatments Timeline**. The edit
dialog opens. To go back to the report you came from, select **Back to Previous
View**.

## Good to know

- The time scrubber and the **APS Decision** card show only on days that have
  AID system data.
- The time scrubber and the **APS Decision** card are not printed.
